{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788127665,"nonce":"1zvBwE+ELTnJsMxpAVquLzT2k1U=","message":"FOLLOW-UP — `rimworld-tools` now has local version control. Session 3.\n\nThis does not change the decision above (`rwa/` and `rwtest/` stay in the\nautorimmer repo). It closes the separate gap that decision exposed: baseviz,\nwhich spec 2.5 reuses, was sitting on an unbacked directory, and an unversioned\ndependency cannot be pinned.\n\n    /home/dorian/projects/rimworld-tools  -\u003e  git repo, 345 files, NO REMOTE\n\n**Local-only, deliberately.** Version control is not publication; the copyright\nconcern that blocked the earlier option only applies to pushing. Nothing is\npushed and no remote is configured. `Info/decompiled/` — decompiled RimWorld\nplus ~60 third-party mods — is gitignored along with the rest of the derived\nbulk (`Info/data`, `perf-mod-analysis`, `soldier-db`, `log-watcher/queue`'s\n6000+ generated reports, backups, `__pycache__`). 467MB on disk, 34MB tracked.\n\n**Correction to what I reported earlier:** I said baseviz and log-watcher were\nboth unbacked. Only baseviz was. `_meta/` and `log-watcher/` are each already\ntheir own local git repo with no remote, so the umbrella ignores them rather\nthan swallowing them as embedded gitlinks — commit inside them, not at the top.\n(It did swallow `_meta` on the first attempt: a `.gitignore` entry written\n`_meta/` with a trailing slash does not match a gitlink, which is a file entry\nnamed `_meta`. Fixed before anything was pushed anywhere, since there is\nnowhere to push.)\n\nSo the genuinely unversioned work was `baseviz/` (52 files), `CEpatches/` (157),\n`bionics-optimizer/` (8), and `Info/`'s scripts and mcp-server (127).\n\nFor whoever takes 2.5: baseviz's catalog and canvas can now be referenced by\ncommit. Vendor-vs-import is still your open question, but \"the dependency has no\nversion to pin\" is no longer an argument for vendoring.","files":null}]}